# Dependencies — installed by `npm install`/`npm ci` from package-lock.json,
# never hand-edited, and enormous (client/node_modules alone was 20,955
# files, ~190MB of this repo's .git history). Committing it means every
# clone pays that cost, every dependency bump is a multi-thousand-file diff
# (see the last commit before this .gitignore for a live example — a
# 7-package `npm uninstall` touched thousands of tracked files), and nothing
# about it is reviewable as a diff anyway. Keep the lockfile committed; drop
# the tree it generates.
node_modules/

# Local environment files. May hold real credentials depending on what a
# future .env adds — even where today's values are low-sensitivity, secrets
# shouldn't be trained into the habit of going through git. .env.example
# stays committed as the template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS and editor cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# NOTE: client/dist/ is intentionally committed, not an oversight — see the
# comment in client/vite.config.js. The site is deployed by copying that
# built output directly (no build step on the server), so it has to be in
# version control for that workflow to work.
